# Open Notebook settings for this machine only. To use them:
#   cp .env.template .env
# .env is ignored by git, so nothing in it ends up in the public repo.
# After a change, Start it again (in the menu: its box → Start) to apply it.
#
# Everything here is optional. The first Start adds two random keys at the end
# of .env, and creates .env for them if there is none:
#   OPEN_NOTEBOOK_ENCRYPTION_KEY  encrypts the API keys you add for cloud models
#   SURREAL_PASSWORD              the database's password
# Keep .env together with data/: with other keys, Open Notebook can't open its
# own database or read the API keys it stored.

# Port on this PC (default 8502). Change it if something else already uses it.
#OPENNOTEBOOK_PORT=8502

# A password for Open Notebook's page. Without one there is no login, which is
# fine while only this PC can open it. Set one before opening it to your
# network.
#OPEN_NOTEBOOK_PASSWORD=

# Who can open Open Notebook:
#   127.0.0.1  this PC only (default, also used when there is no .env)
#   0.0.0.0    also other devices on your network, e.g. a laptop at home.
#              Set OPEN_NOTEBOOK_PASSWORD first, and OPENNOTEBOOK_URL below.
#OPENNOTEBOOK_BIND_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1

# The address other devices open it at, e.g. http://192.168.1.20:8502 (this
# PC's address on your network). The page sends its requests there, so only
# set it together with OPENNOTEBOOK_BIND_ADDRESS=0.0.0.0.
#OPENNOTEBOOK_URL=http://localhost:8502

# --- First start only ---
# The first start points Open Notebook at the stack's engines and picks these
# models from Ollama (Models › Downloaders › Ollama → Sync models builds both).
# After that, change them in Open Notebook under Manage › Models.
#OPENNOTEBOOK_CHAT_MODEL=agent/qwen3.6:35b
#OPENNOTEBOOK_EMBEDDING_MODEL=rag/qwen3-embedding:8b

# How much text Ollama's models keep in mind, in tokens. Open Notebook would
# ask Ollama for 8192 otherwise. 32768 fits any of the stack's models on a
# 32 GB card; agent/qwen3.6:35b holds 262144 there.
#OPENNOTEBOOK_OLLAMA_CONTEXT=32768

# --- Add-ons ---
# How many sources or podcasts Open Notebook works on at once (default 1 here,
# so a local engine gets one request after another).
#OPEN_NOTEBOOK_WORKER_MAX_TASKS=1

# Docling reads scanned PDFs and images better than the built-in reader. It
# installs inside the container on the next Start, downloading several GB from
# pypi.org and huggingface.co. (The stack's own Docling service can't be used:
# Open Notebook only runs Docling inside its own container.)
#OPEN_NOTEBOOK_ENABLE_DOCLING=true

# Any other Open Notebook environment variable also works here, such as cloud
# API keys, though Manage › Models in Open Notebook is the usual place for those.
